{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948010-why-do-prometheans-have-transmutations","id":948010,"title":"Why do Prometheans have Transmutations?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-10T13:38:39-07:00","id":948010,"title":"Why do Prometheans have Transmutations?","content":"I'm not sure I understand why Prometheans have kewl powerz when their goal is to become human.<br /> <br /> Vampire Disciplines and Werewolf Gifts, in universe, help them hunt, Mummy powers help them defend tombs and chase relics, Demon powers help them hide from angels, but it doesn't seem there's a purpose for Transmutations, especially now that they're so transient because of their ties to Refinements which change often.<br /> <br /> It seems odd if it's just 'to defend against Pandorans'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:48:30-07:00","id":948021,"title":"","content":"I think there's a more complex answer than this, and I'll leave it to others to make it, but part of it is that Prometheans <i>are </i>alchemy. Philosophical Refinements inexorably change what they're capable of physically. They can't help but have these powers.<br /> <br /> From a simpler perspective, Promethean powers are all about surviving. They help Prometheans defend against humanity and the elements just as well as they do Pandorans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:51:31-07:00","id":948023,"title":"","content":"Because they are unstable vessels of alchemical potency whose refinement of perception and individuality reflects in their spiritual and physical make-up? And to facilitate survival in face of the inimical circumstances they are sometimes surrounded by as a consequence of their nature, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:52:18-07:00","id":948024,"title":"","content":"Like Mages, Prometheans use their powers to not only survive in a hostile world, but use them as tools to dissect aspects of humanity and the world to increase their understanding of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:54:17-07:00","id":948026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948010-why-do-prometheans-have-transmutations#post948010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I understand why Prometheans have kewl powerz when their goal is to become human.<br /> <br /> Vampire Disciplines and Werewolf Gifts, in universe, help them hunt, Mummy powers help them defend tombs and chase relics, Demon powers help them hide from angels, but it doesn't seem there's a purpose for Transmutations, especially now that they're so transient because of their ties to Refinements which change often.<br /> <br /> It seems odd if it's just 'to defend against Pandorans'</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do those various splats have their powers?<br /> <br /> They do help Vampires and werewolves hunt, but is that why they have them? For vampires, it makes sense that they have them because they help them hunt (or more generally survive), Requiem takes a semi-mystical evolutionary stance on vampires. So vampires with effective Disciplines Embrace and make more with those Disciplines.<br /> <br /> But Werewolf Gifts, is that the same? Depends on the type of gift, wolf gifts yeah, those are evolutionary, moon gifts are cause Luna says so, and shadow gifts are given by spirits after a conscious choice by the werewolf. The wolf must hunt, so most of them tie to hunting, but not all do.<br /> <br /> Mummies have them as you said because they were created to have them, they were designed to guard tombs and chase relics (in universe, I mean).<br /> <br /> Demon's have powers because the nature of reality is that these things exist, Demons use them to hide or fight angels, but the exist anyway as Angles use the same things too (even if they don't really think of it the same way).<br /> <br /> As for Prometheans, because the Principle wants them too? Because the principle is a primal force of change and having the ability to transform yourself embodies that? Because the ability to stretch your bounds and transform yourself is required for the Pilgrimage to even begin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:55:01-07:00","id":948028,"title":"","content":"Transmuations also are &quot;proofs&quot; of the Refinements effects, evidence of a philosophy's metaphysical tangentialness, that the formula not only has impact on thoughts, but on the material world, and therefore on the inner spirit. They show that the formula works, as it were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:01:46-07:00","id":948035,"title":"","content":"Transmutations allow the Created to tap into the inherently chaotic nature of Pyros to warp themselves and help them survive a long, dangerous Pilgrimage in a dark world that challenges and rejects them at every turn. Whether providing the strength to fend off a horde of hungry Pandorans or make a stronger impression on a human being they want to get to know, Transmutations are the consolation prizes they get to make up for the lack of a true soul and the tools to help them reach the New Dawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:21:36-07:00","id":948064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948010-why-do-prometheans-have-transmutations?p=948021#post948021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can't help but have these powers...They help Prometheans defend against humanity and the elements just as well as they do Pandorans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solid answer. Thanks everyone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:34:58-07:00","id":948073,"title":"","content":"Transmutations are expressions of the changes wrought by Refinements. They're not exactly &quot;for&quot; anything, it's just the nature of alchemy. The Pilgrimage is a process of changing one's self, and for creatures as mercurial as Prometheans, to change <i>who</i> one is, is to change <i>what</i> one is. As well as being a result of the nature of the Divine Fire, this fact is part of the metaphysics of the greater Chronicles of Darkness, where the symbolic has very real impact on the literal. Werewolves treat with animistic alien entities governed by the laws of symbolism, Mages shape reality by calling upon symbolic truths that define reality, Changelings literally transform themselves when they change their narrative role, and Prometheans reshape their bodies just as they reshape their souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:58:25-07:00","id":948147,"title":"","content":"From an OOC standpoint, I find it rather odd that we'd be playing a supernatural monster without powers. I mean, I want to play an electrically charged Frankenstein, a golem with a body of stone, a scholar of the Divine Fire that uses actual divine flames. So what if the game turns you human? That's pretty much &quot;Game Over, Good Ending.&quot; That doesn't mean I shouldn't have fun playing with powers in the chronicle before then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T18:41:59-07:00","id":948235,"title":"","content":"Transmutations are practice for the New Dawn. You don't just go up to the mountaintop, call yourself a little Firestorm and walk back down as a mortal. No, you gotta learn how to change everything first. Might not make sense now, why electricity leaps at your command, or why the Disquiet never settles fast on you, but when you're trying to get your dead-ass brain to hold a charge and run your newly alive body, you'll understand. You can't just will it so, any more than you can just fly, but you learn how to make your body change shape, or spew acid, or shine like a lantern, and you start to see how the Fire can work miracles. And when you know how miracles are done, ain't nothing can stop you from doing the only one you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T18:55:11-07:00","id":948251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948010-why-do-prometheans-have-transmutations#post948010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I understand why Prometheans have kewl powerz when their goal is to become human.<br /> <br /> Vampire Disciplines and Werewolf Gifts, in universe, help them hunt, Mummy powers help them defend tombs and chase relics, Demon powers help them hide from angels, but it doesn't seem there's a purpose for Transmutations, especially now that they're so transient because of their ties to Refinements which change often.<br /> <br /> It seems odd if it's just 'to defend against Pandorans'</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're walking, breathing engines of divine fire that cause such effects when harnessed into human flesh. It's the whole thing behind Alchemists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T20:14:04-07:00","id":948302,"title":"","content":"Everyone's pretty much answered it already, but I'm going to coach it in the language of alchemy. <br /> <br /> Mage draws heavily on the gnostic theme &quot;As above, so below.&quot; That is also an alchemical statement, but it is only one half of the alchemical statement. The other half &quot;As within, so without.&quot; As the alchemical process of becoming human works away on Prometheans, they change the world around them, not voluntarily, but imparatively. Alchemically, they must do it, and while Transmutions are not the only manifestation of this, it is one of them. The reverse is also true. When they use Transmutions, it alters, nay refines the Promethean within. As with any alchemy, this is a slow process that you can't just jump to the end of, it takes a lot of purifying and cooking to make a human being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T23:01:12-07:00","id":948391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948010-why-do-prometheans-have-transmutations?p=948147#post948147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From an OOC standpoint, I find it rather odd that we'd be playing a supernatural monster without powers. I mean, I want to play an electrically charged Frankenstein, a golem with a body of stone, a scholar of the Divine Fire that uses actual divine flames. So what if the game turns you human? That's pretty much &quot;Game Over, Good Ending.&quot; That doesn't mean I shouldn't have fun playing with powers in the chronicle before then.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the answer I've always read into the 1e version of a few gamelines and it's one that I can't get past. Having a particular set of mechanics for the sake of just having them seems to demonstrate the sheer pointlessness of playing the game, to me, because it clearly doesn't have enough supportive cohesion to even flesh itself out properly.<br /> <br /> It's fine for supernatural splats to have superpowers, but I want my characters to be able to comprehend them as natural extensions of who and what they are, rather than have them just be carrots for players to enjoy themselves with in between story moments.<br /> <br /> This thread has been helpful for me, too; an answer to this question is one of the things I had hoped for in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T01:32:13-07:00","id":948441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948010-why-do-prometheans-have-transmutations?p=948147#post948147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From an OOC standpoint, I find it rather odd that we'd be playing a supernatural monster without powers. I mean, I want to play an electrically charged Frankenstein, a golem with a body of stone, a scholar of the Divine Fire that uses actual divine flames. So what if the game turns you human? That's pretty much &quot;Game Over, Good Ending.&quot; That doesn't mean I shouldn't have fun playing with powers in the chronicle before then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, that was meant to go without saying. I'm a monster so I get cool powers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T03:22:39-07:00","id":948477,"title":"","content":"Then that should answer the question. I mean, when you're a living machine powered by the essence of a godly being, that's pretty much justification to have any kind of magic, technology or miracle. Any explanation can be given, really. Anything more than that should be explored as an in-game mystery to solve and research. In fact, its kind of the whole point of the Mercurius Refinement and their study of Pyros. And that answer should depend on what kind of answer your current story needs, and change depending on what other stories or other chronicles need.<br /> <br /> Mysteries and questioning the nature of the supernatural is the bread and butter of the Chronicles of Darkness. There shouldn't be easy and universal answers to this kind of thing beyond the most general. Is it part of a grand design from the Principle? Is it a side effect of the ever changing nature of pyros? There's always been a theme running through the abilities to amke them a general extension of the nature of Azoth. The rest is open to be solved as a story hook.<br /> <br /> To me, I'm reading your first post as &quot;Well, you <i>lose</i> everything eventually, so why should you get anything in the first place?&quot; That's kind of a defeatist attitude, imho. Prometheans have powers because its the journey that matters, and they're learning and growing. That learning and growing is reflected in new abilities. They use said abilities throughout the game, because PtC is more than fighting off pandorans and mingling with humans. Promethean is a game about -understanding- your nature, and its only natural to develop abilities based around that knowledge. We're talking about alchemical experiements of your own, about learning what it means to survive in the wilds, about what it means to understand, and surpass, the biological limitations of your body.<br /> <br /> PtC questions human nature. And human nature has a LOT of territory that it covers. Your physical body, personal psychology, sociology (interactions with people), scientific exploration, religion, understanding natural cycles, and more. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948010-why-do-prometheans-have-transmutations?p=948391#post948391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a particular set of mechanics for the sake of just having them seems to demonstrate the sheer pointlessness of playing the game, to me, because it clearly doesn't have enough supportive cohesion to even flesh itself out properly.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sorry, but that's entirely you. The game has never been pointless, and it always had cohesion. From what I've seen, nothing really new has come into 2e beyond tweaking the mechanics. Even alchemists are just a remake of old concepts from another angle. Oh, there's always been questionable parts (I still think the fire/lightning themes with attempts at elemental Lineages is crap), but the answers in this thread you like are the same thing people have said about 1e. There's no difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-11-2016, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}